yes(441,'D','Concentrated nitric acid oxidises copper to copper(II) nitrate and is reduced mainly to nitrogen dioxide. The balanced equation is Cu + 4HNO₃ → Cu(NO₃)₂ + 2NO₂ + 2H₂O.',['https://www2.chem.wisc.edu/deptfiles/genchem/demonstrations/Gen_Chem_Pages/04chemrxnpage/nitric_acid_acts_on_copper.htm'],question='Copper reacts with concentrated nitric acid to give which set of products?',options=['Cu(NO₃)₃, NO, N₂O₄ and H₂O','Cu(NO₃)₂, NO and H₂O','CuO, NO₂ and H₂O','Cu(NO₃)₂, NO₂ and H₂O'],check='copper-nitric-balance')
