yes(443,'B','Aluminium oxide reacts with sulfuric acid and also with sodium hydroxide. An oxide that reacts with both acids and bases is amphoteric.',[RX],question='Al₂O₃(s) + 3H₂SO₄(aq) → Al₂(SO₄)₃(aq) + 3H₂O(l). Al₂O₃(s) + 2NaOH(aq) + 3H₂O(l) → 2NaAl(OH)₄(aq). These reactions show that Al₂O₃ is',check='amphoteric-balances')
