yes(445,'D','The longest carbon chain has six atoms. Numbering from the end nearer the first branch puts methyl groups at positions 2 and 4, rather than 3 and 5. The name is 2,4-dimethylhexane.',[ORG],question='What is the IUPAC name of CH₃CH(CH₃)CH₂CH(CH₃)CH₂CH₃?',options=['Dimethylhexane','3,5-dimethylpentane','1,1-dimethyl-3-methylpentane','2,4-dimethylhexane'],audit='Visually restored the two methyl branches from PDF39; preserved all distractor identities while normalising spelling/punctuation.',check='hexane-graph')
yes(446,'B','Tetraethyllead improves resistance to engine knocking, but burning leaded fuel releases lead-containing pollution in the exhaust. This environmental contamination is the reason for avoiding it as an antiknock additive.',['https://www.epa.gov/lead/lead-air','https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2020-11/documents/lead.pdf'],question='Why is tetraethyllead undesirable as an antiknock additive?',options=['It is expensive','It causes pollution through exhaust emissions','It lowers the octane rating of petrol','It is explosive'])
