yes(456,'D','Down a group, additional electron shells increase shielding and the distance between the nucleus and bonding electrons. Electronegativity therefore generally decreases. Atomic size and electropositivity generally increase.',['https://openstax.org/books/chemistry-2e/pages/6-5-periodic-variations-in-element-properties'],question='Which of these properties generally decreases down a group in the periodic table?',options=['Atomic radius','Ionic radius','Electropositivity','Electronegativity'],audit='Removed next-question electron diagram text from D and corrected grammar; stated periodic trend as general rather than exception-free.')
