yes(458,'C','Deuterium is hydrogen-2. A neutral deuterium atom has one proton, one neutron and one electron, giving mass number 2 and atomic number 1.',[ATOM],question='Which option gives the numbers of protons, neutrons and electrons, respectively, in a neutral deuterium atom?',options=['1, 0, 0','1, 0, 1','1, 1, 1','1, 2, 1'],audit='Restored all three table columns from visually inspected PDF41. Corrected old B to C using isotope definition; PDF41 re-inspected: A(1,0,0), B(1,0,1), C(1,1,1), D(1,2,1) are fully visible. Removed unavailable TeamBoma3969 corroboration; source recovery rests on supplied PDF.',check='deuterium-table')
